joularcore=0.0.4: Library to monitor hardware components' energy consumption on all OSes
Origin: commit 094fe453bbcfc64307e83b54aac218c3ae4d33fc from https://github.com/joular/joularcore.git
Available when: (case OS is Linux => True, Macos => True, Windows => True, others => False)
Properties:
   Author: Adel Noureddine
   Description: Library to monitor hardware components' energy consumption on all OSes
   GPR Scenario: JOULARCORE_LIBRARY_TYPE := static | relocatable | static-pic
   GPR Scenario: PJ_OS := linux | windows | macos
   case OS is
      when Linux => GPR External: PJ_OS := linux
      when Macos => GPR External: PJ_OS := macos
      when Windows => GPR External: PJ_OS := windows
   License: LGPL-3.0-only
   Long_Description: Joular Core measures the energy or power consumption of hardware components:
CPU (Intel and AMD through RAPL on Linux and Windows, Apple Silicon and Intel Macs through powermetrics, Raspberry Pi and other boards through power models) and
GPU (Nvidia through NVML, AMD through hwmon sysfs or ADLX, Apple Silicon through
powermetrics). It detects on its own what the machine offers, and also provides
a C interface so any language with a C FFI can use it.

   Maintainer: Adel Noureddine <adel.noureddine@outlook.com>
